    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **51 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp37Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field that renders the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving the raw `telephone` field as E.164.\n\nThree changes, following the existing derived-field pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`, `initials`, etc.). The generated `OwnerDto` picks up the new field at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/TelephoneDisplays.java`** (new) \u2014 a plain static helper (mirroring `Localities`) that formats `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`: it splits the country code using a recognised-codes table (`61`, `1`), then groups the national digits in threes. Returns `null` for null/blank/malformed input.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = ...)` that calls the helper on `owner.getTelephone()`, consistent with how the other derived fields are populated.\n\nThe raw `telephone` mapping is untouched, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns both `\"telephone\": \"+61412345678\"` and `\"telephoneDisplay\": \"+61 412 345 678\"`.",
